    "excerpt": "Are diagram rings phrase tables for the text? (Re's \"mad-lib\" idea) Word pairs that sit next to each other in the 119 diagram rings occur next to each other in running text 1.69 times as often as when ring order is shuffled. Control: ordinary held-out paragraph lines score 1.66. The rings behave exactly like ordinary text, so this test gives no evidence that they are look-up tables. It cannot rule out a procedure whose tables and output are both text-like."
